   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to a report by the division for\nsmall business",
    "basePrintNo": "S7820",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7820-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §170-c, Exec L (as proposed in S.6642-A & A.7500)",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7820\n\nSPONSOR: KAPLAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to a report by the divi-\nsion for small business\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment to L.2021, c.752, to clarify provisions\nconcerning the Executive Law.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends several provisions of L.2021, c.752.\n\nSection 1 amends the Executive Law by amending the annual date which\nagencies must provide information covering the previous calendar year to\nthe Division for Small Business, from March first to July first follow-\ning the effective date of this bill and every July first thereafter.\n\nThis section also amends the type of information to be provided to the\nDivision for Small Business to include the range of time, rather than\nthe average length of time, granted by the state agency to correct first\ntime violations and adds that the type of violations that were amelio-\nrated be included in the reported information.\n\nThis bill also amends the subdivision by amending the date for which the\nagency must prepare an annual report compiling this information from May\nfirst to October first following the effective date of this bill and\nevery October first thereafter.\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately with information to be provided\nto the Division for Small Business by March first and agency reports to\nbe prepared by October first following the effective date of this bill.\nThis act is set to expire on December 20, 2024.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 762 of the Laws of 2021. S.6642-A passed\nthe Senate in June 2021, and A.7500 passed the Assembly in May 2021.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately on the same date and in the same\nmanner as a chapter of the laws of 2021 amending the administrative\nprocedure act, as proposed in legislative bills S.6642-A and A.7500 take\neffect, and expire on December 20, 2024.\n",
